//
// The LM-head GEMV's re-execution gate. `[2026-08-21]` The production
// 19 x 8192 `lm_head_gemv` multi-launch ELF returns wrong, non-deterministic
// values in partition 0 whenever it executes immediately after itself (doc 57
// section 1.4, devq 446-448; confirmed on the production artifact, devq 452:
// 5 of 7 dispatches wrong, healed only by running another ELF in between, NOT
// by a 0.5 s idle). Production decode never places the head next to itself
// and `make verify` judges token sets, so neither can see it; this gate
// compiles the production builder's module fresh and dispatches it seven
// times in the patterns that expose it. The defect is OPEN: the lit is
// expected to FAIL, and a fix anywhere from builder to device turns it into
// an XPASS -- drop the XFAIL line then, and the gate is green on the fix.
//
// No HF weights: random weights against an f32 reference. NPU serialization
// lives one layer down (KernelCache takes /tmp/npu.lock).
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano
// XFAIL: *
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_npu2_lm_head_reexec
// RUN: cd test_npu2_lm_head_reexec
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile check-lm-head-reexec PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR | FileCheck %s
//
// CHECK: [reexec] d1 first dispatch: clean
// CHECK: [reexec] d2 back-to-back: clean
// CHECK: [reexec] d3 back-to-back: clean
// CHECK: [reexec] d4 after 0.5 s idle: clean
// CHECK: [reexec] d5 new input back-to-back: clean
// CHECK: [reexec] d6 after other ELF: clean
// CHECK: [reexec] d7 back-to-back after d6: clean
// CHECK: [reexec] PASS
